    affiliation: "Universite Cote d'Azur, CEPAM; Universite de Geneve, Faculte de Theologie Jean Calvin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/romain-girardi-eng/EleutherIA"
url: "https://free-will.app"
abstract: >-
  EleutherIA is an open scholarly research platform and FAIR-aligned
  knowledge graph for ancient debates on free will, fate, moral
  responsibility, and agency across the Greco-Roman and early Christian
  worlds. This release combines a curated knowledge graph, an ancient-text
  corpus, and an agentic GraphRAG stack for citation-grounded question
  answering, graph exploration, and data quality auditing. As of the
  2026-06-05 KG snapshot bundled with this release, the graph contains
  20,060 nodes, 56,737 edges, and 19,751 passage citations over 241 ancient
  works and ~17,800 anchored passages in Greek and Latin (with English
  translations); the RDF export carries 560,110 triples with per-edge
  provenance. Version 5.1.0 adds enforced answer-time verification:
  a deterministic quote-fidelity gate, a corpus-backed ancient-text
  verifier, an adversarial per-claim citation auditor, a golden evaluation
  harness in CI, and corpus tamper-evidence tooling. All counts are
  machine-generated from the dataset snapshots (scripts/gen_stats.py,
  data/stats.json).
